2. FORMAL SYSTEM DEFINITION

Definition 2.1 (PCMSA Body). A PCMSA robotic body \mathcal{B} is the five‑tuple

\mathcal{B} = (S_m, A_e, C_p, \Phi, \Theta)

where
S_m = \{M_i\}_{i=1}^{N_s} – hollow composite skeletal modules, each occupying a domain \Omega_i \subset \mathbb{R}^3 with anisotropic stiffness \mathbf{C}^{(i)} and density \rho_i(\mathbf{x});
A_e = \{(\text{coil}_j,\text{magnet}_j,\text{gap}_j)\}_{j=1}^{N_a} – distributed actuators, each a microcoil plus NdFeB Halbach source;
C_p = \{\text{wg}_l, \text{src}_l, \text{det}_l\}_{l=1}^{N_p} – photonic channels, each a polymer waveguide with source‑detector pair;
\Phi : S_m \times A_e \to \mathbb{R}^3 – field‑coupling map returning the magnetic flux density at each structural node;
\Theta : C_p \times S_m \to \mathbb{R}^{N_p} – photonic readout mapping waveguide deformations to optical intensities.

Definition 2.2 (Admissible State Space).

X_{\mathcal{B}} = \Big\{ (\mathbf{u}, \mathbf{B}_{\text{field}}, \mathbf{I}_{\text{opt}}) \in H^1(\Omega)\times L^2(\Omega;\mathbb{R}^3)\times \mathbb{R}^{N_p} \;\Big|\;
\sigma_{ij}(\mathbf{u})n_j = f_i^{\text{surface}} \text{ on } \partial\Omega_N,\; \mathbf{u}=0 \text{ on } \partial\Omega_D,

\nabla\cdot\mathbf{B}_{\text{field}}=0,\; |\mathbf{B}_{\text{field}}|\le B_{\text{sat}},\; I_{\text{opt},k} \ge I_{\text{noise}} \;\forall k \Big\}.

