Appendix G: Power Budget and Scalability

G.1 Single Module Power Budget

For one actuator module: continuous current I_c = 1\,\text{A}, coil resistance R_c = 2\,\Omega, Joule loss P_J = 2\,\text{W}. The Halbach holding force requires no steady‑state power. Photonics: LED source power <5\,\text{mW} per channel. Quiescent power per module <2.1\,\text{W}. Peak transient power (overload) can reach 10\,\text{W} for <1\,\text{s}.

G.2 Arm‑Level Scalability

A 7‑DOF arm with an average of two actuator modules per joint yields N_a = 14 actuator units. Total sustained electrical power P_{\text{total}} \approx 14 \times 2 = 28\,\text{W}. With a 100 Wh battery, continuous operation time >3.5\,\text{h}. The structural mass of modules and couplings scales roughly linearly with DOF, avoiding the exponential escalation seen in geared designs.

